 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Over six hundred thousand customers without power. And a century-old parade has moved."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Cape May first. On Thursday morning, its tide gauge beat a record set in a January twenty sixteen blizzard, Fox Weather reports. North Wildwood police said no car could enter or leave the town. New Jersey's governor declared an emergency in all twenty-one counties."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Then the wind. More than six hundred thousand customers lost power on Thanksgiving Day, CNN reports, citing PowerOutage dot U S. New Jersey's governor warned some outages could last into the weekend. And more than three hundred sixty flights were cancelled."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "In New York, the hundredth Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade moved to Saturday. CNN calls it the first postponement in the parade's history. City rules ground the giant balloons when gusts top thirty-four miles per hour. Macy's says it decided with the city."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the hundredth parade march on Saturday? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
