 "upload": {
  "title": "Thanksgiving Storm Sets a Cape May Tide Record #shorts",
  "description": "A powerful Thanksgiving storm hit the U.S. East Coast. Cape May's tide gauge beat a record from a January 2016 blizzard, Fox Weather reports (preliminary), and North Wildwood police said no vehicles could enter or leave the town. More than 600,000 customers lost power on Thanksgiving Day, according to PowerOutage.us via CNN, and the 100th Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade was moved to Saturday, the first postponement in its history according to CNN.\n\nSources: Fox Weather; 6abc; CNN; The Washington Post; CBS News; The Hill; Fox News (based on search-result excerpts). Flood areas and the parade route on the map are approximate and illustrative.\n\n#climate #weather #thanksgiving #noreaster #coastalflooding",
